.Dd September 16, 2026
.Dt NDI_SET_BUS_PRIVATE 9F
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndi_set_bus_private ,
.Nm ndi_get_bus_private ,
.Nm ndi_port_type
.Nd access bus-private data associated with a device node
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/sunndi.h
.Ft "void"
.Fo ndi_set_bus_private
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "boolean_t up"
.Fa "uint32_t port_type"
.Fa "void *data"
.Fc
.Ft "void *"
.Fo ndi_get_bus_private
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "boolean_t up"
.Fc
.Ft "boolean_t"
.Fo ndi_port_type
.Fa "dev_info_t *dip"
.Fa "boolean_t up"
.Fa "uint32_t port_type"
.Fc
.Sh INTERFACE LEVEL
illumos specific
.Pq Consolidation Private .
.Sh PARAMETERS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Va dip
Device node containing the slots.
.It Va up
\fBB_TRUE\fP for upstream, or \fBB_FALSE\fP for downstream.
.It Va port_type
Bus-framework-defined type tag.
.It Va data
Bus-private pointer to store; may be \fBNULL\fP.
.El
.Sh DESCRIPTION
Each device node has separate upstream and downstream bus-private slots.
\fBup\fP selects the upstream slot when true and the downstream slot when false.
\fBndi_set_bus_private()\fP stores \fBdata\fP and its \fBport_type\fP tag in that slot.
\fBndi_get_bus_private()\fP returns the stored pointer, and \fBndi_port_type()\fP
tests the associated type tag.
.Pp
The data is neither copied nor freed by these functions.
The bus framework owns its allocation and lifetime.
These slots are distinct from the driver-private pointer accessed through
\fBddi_get_driver_private()\fP.
Callers must keep \fBdip\fP and the stored object valid and serialize concurrent
updates; these functions acquire no locks.
.Sh CONTEXT
These functions may be called from user, kernel, or interrupt context
with the necessary caller-supplied synchronization.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
\fBndi_get_bus_private()\fP returns the stored pointer, which is initially
\fBNULL\fP.
\fBndi_port_type()\fP returns \fBB_TRUE\fP for a matching tag and \fBB_FALSE\fP otherwise.
\fBndi_set_bus_private()\fP has no return value.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ddi_get_driver_private 9F ,
.Xr ndi_flavorv_alloc 9F ,
.Xr sunndi 9F
